Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:11:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?HTDESIGNER-49:=20=E6=94=B9=E5=90=8D=E7=A8=B1=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?(F2)=20--=20a=20component's=20name=20(id),=20like=20WPF's=20Nam?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20field=20(0.49.0)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

F2 on the design surface, the pencil by the name at the top of the
properties panel, or right-click 改名稱: the selected component's id changes
on the page -- its start tag and the generated title="name : TClass" (one
edit), every <label for>, and, as BCB6 does, its caption when that still is
the old name (a new Label1 showing "Label1"). One undo step; the renamed
one stays selected.
- the new name must be a BCB6 name (letters, digits, _; not starting with a
  digit) and not taken on the page
- a name the .dfm has, or one the page's JS uses, is asked about first: those
  links are not renamed (the DFM comparison, events, C++ and the web code
  stay as they are)
- lib/htmlblock.renameEdits (a child's own caption is never touched)

Fix found on the way: after a structural edit, a late 'select' from the page
before the redraw could reset the name the redrawn page selects (the
renamed / new component). Until the new page is ready such an answer no
longer changes it.

Tests: lib (renameEdits on HotPlate and made-up checkbox / panel markup),
smoke (spbSave is in the DFM: asked; closed = nothing; answered = renamed,
id + title, selected; a bad and a taken name refused), panels_render (the
pencil posts rename), real VS Code (spbSave -> btnSaveX in the source and
the tree, selected, ONE undo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
